
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Computer Ports Guide</title>
<style>
body{font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background:#eaf7ff;color:#19334a;margin:0;padding:25px}
header{text-align:center;background:#168aad;color:white;padding:25px;border-radius:16px}
main{max-width:850px;margin:25px auto}
.port{background:white;margin:15px 0;padding:20px;border-radius:12px;border-left:6px solid #168aad}
h2{margin-top:0}
.tag{background:#d5f2ff;padding:5px 10px;border-radius:20px;font-size:13px}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header><h1>🔌 Computer Ports Guide</h1><p>Discover how devices connect to computers.</p></header>
<main>
<div class="port"><h2>USB Port</h2><span class="tag">Data and Power</span><p>Connects keyboards, mice, storage drives and other devices.</p></div>
<div class="port"><h2>HDMI Port</h2><span class="tag">Audio and Video</span><p>Connects a computer to a monitor, television or projector.</p></div>
<div class="port"><h2>Ethernet Port</h2><span class="tag">Networking</span><p>Provides a wired network connection using an Ethernet cable.</p></div>
<div class="port"><h2>Audio Jack</h2><span class="tag">Sound</span><p>Connects compatible headphones, speakers or microphones.</p></div>
<div class="port"><h2>USB-C Port</h2><span class="tag">Versatile Connection</span><p>Can support charging, data transfer and video, depending on the device.</p></div>
<div class="port"><h2>DisplayPort</h2><span class="tag">Display</span><p>Connects computers to compatible monitors for digital video and audio.</p></div>
</main>
</body>
</html>
